    "result_text": "The full suite is green (BUILD SUCCESS, 2 tests, 0 failures).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented telephone normalization on owner creation in `ValidateOwnerFields.java` \u2014 the first step of the `POST /api/owners` OfficeFloor pipeline.\n\n**How it works:**\n- The pipeline binds `@RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto` *without* `@Valid`, so the DTO's generated `^[0-9]*$` pattern is not enforced at binding \u2014 the raw string (e.g. `\"(04) 1234-5678\"`) reaches the validation step intact.\n- Added a `normalizeTelephone(...)` helper that strips every non-digit character (`replaceAll(\"\\\\D\", \"\")`):\n  - Exactly 10 digits \u2192 writes the normalized value back onto the request via `setTelephone(...)`, so `BuildOwner` \u2192 `SaveOwner` persist and `RespondWithOwnerCreated`/`GET` return the 10-digit form.\n  - Anything else \u2192 adds a `\"telephone\"` error, which the existing `OwnerFieldsInvalidException` handler turns into a **400**.\n- The `contains` guard avoids a duplicate `\"telephone\"` error when the field is also blank.\n\nThis satisfies both new acceptance tests: `\"(04) 1234-5678\"` stores/returns `\"0412345678\"`, and `\"12345\"` is rejected with 400. No other steps or YAML wiring needed changing.",
